Package: fzd
Version: @VERSION@
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Sean Patrick <17012946+seanap@users.noreply.github.com>
Depends: plocate, bash (>= 4.4), fzf (>= 0.44.0), zoxide (>= 0.9.0), coreutils (>= 8.28), findutils (>= 4.6), util-linux (>= 2.31), grep (>= 3.1), sed (>= 4.4), mawk | gawk, micro
Recommends: python3, eza, fd-find, bat, file, tree, libglib2.0-bin | trash-cli
Suggests: chafa, glow, wl-clipboard, xclip, zsh, zsh-autosuggestions
Homepage: https://github.com/seanap/fzd
Description: fast keyboard-driven terminal file explorer
 FZD combines Bash and fzf for fuzzy navigation, previews, global search,
 directory history and safe single-item file operations. Linux Trash is
 available with gio or trash-put; permanent deletion is never substituted.
 .
 Source /usr/share/fzd/integration.sh in Bash or zsh to enable directory
 return through fzd_cd/fzd_find, and lf/lff when those command names are free.
